Not from Solaris: OpenIndiana-only.

Solaris gives the greeter user gdm its own PAM stack through user_attr's
pam_policy=/etc/gdm/gdm-launch-environment.pam (auth pam_allow).  illumos
has no pam_policy and reads only /etc/pam.conf, which packages cannot amend.
OpenIndiana's pam.conf does carry a gdm-autologin stack (auth
pam_unix_cred + pam_allow, account pam_allow), the same stack Solaris uses
for the greeter, so the greeter's PAM conversation uses that service name.
The worker keeps "gdm-launch-environment" as its service everywhere else.

--- a/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
+++ b/daemon/gdm-session-worker.c
@@ -1425,7 +1425,11 @@
         pam_conversation.appdata_ptr = worker;
 
         gdm_session_worker_start_auditor (worker);
-        error_code = pam_start (service,
+        /* illumos: no pam_policy in user_attr, and pam.conf cannot be
+         * amended by packages; the greeter uses OpenIndiana's existing
+         * gdm-autologin stack (pam_allow), as Solaris' greeter policy does. */
+        error_code = pam_start (strcmp (service, "gdm-launch-environment") == 0 ?
+                                    "gdm-autologin" : service,
                                 username,
                                 &pam_conversation,
                                 &worker->pam_handle);
